{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1470680-marie-von-junzt","id":1470680,"title":"Marie von Junzt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-16T18:58:57-08:00","id":1470680,"title":"Marie von Junzt","content":"Epitaph: Revenge seeking Nazi occultist<br /> <br /> Clan: Gangrel<br /> <br /> Quote: (withering silent stare)<br /> <br /> Mortal Days: Stregoicavar and the Ahnenerbe<br /> <br /> Marie von Junzt came from the village of Stregoicavar as a Danube Swabian (or ethnic German living in Hungry) before the First World War. This is the where and when of her origins, but it does not explain her. Something dark always dwelled at the core of her soul.<br /> <br /> The growing industrialization of the country benefited the von Junzt family. Her father served as a head of a local academy. Her mother enjoyed status as a member of the middle class. One of her brothers worked at a bank and the other brother worked in Budapest. The Great War fell on the village, but combat never approached Stregoicavar. Her brothers served in the war and, in a turn of good fortune, both survived and returned home. But Marie\u2019s personality drifted darker, and she had never been a ray of sunshine.<br /> <br /> Marie found employment as a secretary in the Bulgarian village of Vasaria. There, she experienced a dire vision while visiting the local chapel. This vision came to her of the arc of history and finding purpose in the face of annihilation. Trying to understand the vision, and make its message a part of her life, led her to Germany. Her reputation for competence gained her the attention of Heinrich Himmler and the Nazi party in Berlin. Marie became a secretary and worked most often with Himmler. He created the Ahnenerbe which served as a think tank appendage for the SS. He created a position for von Junzt in the \u00dcberpr\u00fcfung der sogenannten Geheimwissenschaften institute. von Junzt officially remained a secretary, but she actually served as a skilled operative.<br /> Working as a Nazi and pursuing Arian ideals gave von Junzt purpose. It did not give her joy because nothing gave her joy. But the work allowed her to soldier on through the dour joylessness which defined von Junzt life. She continued in this role until an encounter with a vampire in the dying days of the war.<br /> <br /> Vampire Nights: A purpose to the darkness<br /> <br /> It says something about von Junzt will that she survived as an abandoned neonate as Berlin fell before advancing armies at the end of a war. The Allies would have shot von Junzt for her crime if they had caught her as a living woman.<br /> <br /> von Junzt drifted, moving from Germany to Argentina to New England and back to her home village. von Junzt made herself useful to people with power during this period. She also learned to collecting her own followers. von Junzt dedicated her existence to tormenting her sire and pursuing occult knowledge. With the knowledge, she tried to make sense of the vision she endured in that old chapel so many years before. von Junzt had tried to make sense and give purpose to herself and the vision with Arian ideals. But the collapse of Nazi Germany left those ideas in shambles. So she called in some favors to have Neo-Nazi Frederick Werther embraced and made over until he believed himself to be Heinrich Himmler. von Junzt used this catspaw to cause trouble and distractions.<br /> <br /> Things changed for her when she met Marcus Vitel. This is because Vitel revealed things to her, about himself, about the world, and even about von Junzt. Use of Aklo Vitel allowed von Junzt to send a message to her past self. So von Junzt sent a message to herself back in that Vasaria chapel. This allowed her to reconcile with herself that the master race had never been human. As something no longer human, and whom had never been humane, she found this palatable.<br /> <br /> So von Junzt has a new purpose. She serves as an agent of Vitel - whom she calls the Dark One - in a way like how she once served the real Himmler. But now von Juntz goals are even darker and her methods more ruthless.<br /> <br /> Plots and Schemes:<br /> <br /> Beast in the Pit: People are throwing themselves into the Pit because of von Juntz. She is aware of the shub-spawn. von Juntz is attempting to wake the creature because of the damage it will do to Chicago. If von Juntz is successful, the shub-spawn will begin hunting in locations providing ample reflective surfaces. This includes the glass skinned skyscrapers in Chicago and the Cloud Gate at Millennium Park. This would pose a Masquerade breach - people disappearing into thin air - that would be difficult to handle. She also plans on unleashing the creature into the material world.<br /> <br /> von Juntz and Thurber are working together on a work of performance art that should also steadily drive Kindred leadership into madness.<br /> <br /> Domain and Haven:<br /> <br /> Midway Gardens (Haven 2): von Juntz is using the Midway Gardens as a haven while staying in Chicago. This is with the permission of Clarissa Thurber. The two are sharing the domain.<br /> <br /> Thralls and Tools:<br /> <br /> Cult of Personality (Allies 4): Vitel has provided von Juntz a segment of his mortal cult for protection, support and so on. This function has a group of Gifted Mortals (V5 page 185), a couple of whom work at the Jones and Rogers Art Gallery and others work at the Gardens.<br /> <br /> Julian Sandberg (Retainer 3): Thurber is sharing her retainer with von Juntz. Sandberg is also a Gifted Mortal, works as the general manager of the gallery, and knows what Thurber and von Juntz are plotting - he will die to support them.<br /> <br /> Kindred Relationships:<br /> <br /> Her Sire (hatred): Much of von Juntz existence is defined by her hatred for her sire.<br /> <br /> Clarissa Thurber (Useful): von Juntz views Thurber as a useful ally, nothing more and nothing less.<br /> <br /> Vitel (worship): von Juntz worships the thing she calls the Dark One, and who others call Marcus Vitel.<br /> <br /> Whispers:<br /> <br /> Who is this woman? There is gossip in Gangrel circles about this \u201cElsa\u201d and what she wants in the city. The same circles go through Toreador circles based on \u201cElsa\u2019s\u201d relationship with Thurber.<br /> <br /> Mask and Mien:<br /> <br /> von Juntz poses as a German Gangrel named Elsa Altberg-Ehrenstein. She says she will stay in the city for a few months before moving on. Most of the Chicago Kindred say take her at her word.<br /> <br /> Sire: Beckett<br /> <br /> Embraced: 1944 (Born 1914)<br /> <br /> Ambition: The serve a roll in the devastation of the lesser races.<br /> <br /> Convictions: The true master race is not human.<br /> <br /> Touchstones: Her sire - hatred<br /> <br /> Humanity: 1<br /> <br /> Generation: 8th<br /> <br /> Blood Potency: 3<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2; Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 5; Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 5<br /> <br /> Secondary Attributes: Health 5, Willpower 7<br /> <br /> Skills: Drive 2, Melee 2, Firearms 2, Survival 2; Etiquette 2, Insight 1, Intimidation 3, Leadership 4, Performance 2, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2; Academics 3, Finance 1, Occult 4, Politics 3.<br /> <br /> Secondary Attributes: Health 7, Willpower 8<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Auspex 2, Blood Sorcery 4, Obfuscate 1, Presence 1, Protean 2<br /> <br /> Background: Aklo 4, Mawla 5 (Vitel)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 12-17-2021, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-revie